{
  "_comment": "Explicit test-selection overrides layered on top of the automatic consumer graph. Keys and values are matched case-insensitively.",
  "_schema": {
    "include": "Subprojects to add that cannot be derived as same-stage consumers from RUNTIME_DEPS/BUILD_DEPS. Covers: (a) test-only projects with no link-time dep edge (e.g. hip-tests, rocgdb-cpu), (b) same-stage reverse edges not present as forward consumers, and (c) foundational deps that have no derivable build stage (rocm-core, rocm-cmake, ...), whose consumers must be listed explicitly because the same-stage cut selects nothing for them.",
    "exclude": "Subprojects to remove even though they appear as consumers in the graph (e.g. to avoid expensive suites for low-risk changes).",
    "_note_cross_stage": "Cross-stage 'universal' consumers of hip-clr / ROCR-Runtime (~28 each) are intentionally NOT enumerated here. A change to those triggers a broad rebuild; enumerating their consumers would recreate the whole-tree test explosion the bounded same-stage design exists to prevent."
  },

